        (bool ok2, ) = address(c).call{value: 10 ether}("");
        // Reference: succeeds; Bug: reverts because require(block.timestamp > pastBlockTime) fails (200 > 0 is true! Wait, need to check)
        // Actually 200 > 0 is true, so both would succeed. Need different approach.
        // Let's re-think: block.timestamp > pastBlockTime: reference has 101, bug has 0; both pass 200 > 101 and 200 > 0. So this doesn't diverge.
        // Use vm.warp to a time between 0 and 101, e.g., 50: reference fails (50 > 101 false), bug succeeds (50 > 0 true). That's the divergence.
